Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 9.0.6 has been released and is 
available for download.

Apart from small bug fixes, this version improves the use of sadf with 
its -x option (displaying XML output): It is now possible to specify a 
starting and ending time with options -s and -e. Interval and count 
parameters are also taken into account by sadf -x.
Oh, and this version also includes a new tool (sargraph) from Lans 
Carstensen to make graphs based on XML output from sadf!

Sysstat 9.0.6 is available for download from my web page at:
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

293kB sysstat-9.0.6.tar.gz
239kB sysstat-9.0.6.tar.bz2
296kB sysstat-9.0.6-1.src.rpm
272kB sysstat-9.0.6-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://pagesperso-orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 9.0.5 are:
* "sadf -x" now takes into account options -s and -e (which specify a 
starting and ending time) and also interval and count parameters [DEBIAN 
bug#546259].
* Option -C added to sadf. Use it to tell sadf to display comments 
present in file (also works with XML format).
* sar and sadf sometimes didn't handle COMMENT records properly. This is 
now fixed.
* XML output (displayed by sadf -x) modified for kernel tables statistics.
* XSD and DTD documents updated.
* [Yibin Shen]: HZ variable was not explicitly set in sadc.c. This is 
now fixed.
* [Lans Carstensen]: sargraph added (sargraph is a shell script used to 
make graphs based on sadf XML output).
* sadf manual page updated.
* FAQ updated.
* NLS updated.

